equires that SSLv3 not be used.  The replacement versions,\n   in particular Transport Layer Security (TLS) 1.2, are considerably\n   more secure and capable protocols.\n\n   This document updates the backward compatibility sections of the TLS\n   RFCs to prohibit fallback to SSLv3.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-sslv3-diediedie/", "expires": "2015-09-03T00:35:39Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 75680, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-sslv3-diediedie", "note": "", "notify": "\"Joseph A. Salowey\" <joe@salowey.net>", "pages": 6, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/75680/", "rev": "02", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/joe@salowey.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/12/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2015-04-01T16:01:11Z", "title": "Deprecating Secure Sockets Layer Version 3.0", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Secure Sockets Layer version 3.0 (SSLv3) is no longer secure.  This\n   document requires that SSLv3 not be used.  The replacement versions,\n   in particular Transport Layer Security (TLS) 1.2, are considerably\n   more secure and capable protocols.\n\n   This document updates the backward compatibility sections of the TLS\n   RFCs to prohibit fallback to SSLv3.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-sslv3-diediedie/", "expires": "2015-09-03T00:35:39Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 75684, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-sslv3-diediedie", "note": "", "notify": "\"Joseph A. Salowey\" <joe@salowey.net>", "pages": 6, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/75684/", "rev": "02", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/joe@salowey.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/12/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2015-04-01T16:01:11Z", "title": "Deprecating Secure Sockets Layer Version 3.0", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Secure Sockets Layer version 3.0 (SSLv3) is no longer secure.  This\n   document requires that SSLv3 not be used.  The replacement versions,\n   in particular Transport Layer Security (TLS) 1.2, are considerably\n   more secure and capable protocols.\n\n   This document updates the backward compatibility sections of the TLS\n   RFCs to prohibit fallback to SSLv3.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-sslv3-diediedie/", "expires": "2015-09-03T00:35:39Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 75687, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-sslv3-diediedie", "note": "", "notify": "\"Joseph A. Salowey\" <joe@salowey.net>", "pages": 6, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/75687/", "rev": "02", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/joe@salowey.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/12/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2015-04-01T16:01:11Z", "title": "Deprecating Secure Sockets Layer Version 3.0", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Secure Sockets Layer version 3.0 (SSLv3) is no longer secure.  This\n   document requires that SSLv3 not be used.  The replacement versions,\n   in particular Transport Layer Security (TLS) 1.2, are considerably\n   more secure and capable protocols.\n\n   This document updates the backward compatibility sections of the TLS\n   RFCs to prohibit fallback to SSLv3.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-sslv3-diediedie/", "expires": "2015-09-03T00:35:39Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 76037, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-sslv3-diediedie", "note": "", "notify": "\"Joseph A. Salowey\" <joe@salowey.net>", "pages": 6, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/76037/", "rev": "02", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/joe@salowey.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/12/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2015-04-01T16:01:11Z", "title": "Deprecating Secure Sockets Layer Version 3.0", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Secure Sockets Layer version 3.0 (SSLv3) is no longer secure.  This\n   document requires that SSLv3 not be used.  The replacement versions,\n   in particular Transport Layer Security (TLS) 1.2, are considerably\n   more secure and capable protocols.\n\n   This document updates the backward compatibility sections of the TLS\n   RFCs to prohibit fallback to SSLv3.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-sslv3-diediedie/", "expires": "2015-09-03T00:35:39Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 76099, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-sslv3-diediedie", "note": "", "notify": "\"Joseph A. Salowey\" <joe@salowey.net>", "pages": 6, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/76099/", "rev": "02", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/joe@salowey.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/9/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/point/"], "time": "2015-04-09T18:08:18Z", "title": "Deprecating Secure Sockets Layer Version 3.0", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Secure Sockets Layer version 3.0 (SSLv3) [RFC6101] is not\n   sufficiently secure.  This document requires that SSLv3 not be used.\n   The replacement versions, in particular Transport Layer Security\n   (TLS) 1.2 [RFC5246], are considerably more secure and capable\n   protocols.\n\n   This document updates the backward compatibility section of RFC 5246\n   and its predecessors to prohibit fallback to SSLv3.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-sslv3-diediedie/", "expires": "2015-10-12T19:46:09Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 76172, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-sslv3-diediedie", "note": "", "notify": "\"Joseph A. Salowey\" <joe@salowey.net>", "pages": 6, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/76172/", "rev": "03", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/joe@salowey.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/9/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/point/"], "time": "2015-04-10T19:46:09Z", "title": "Deprecating Secure Sockets Layer Version 3.0", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Secure Sockets Layer version 3.0 (SSLv3) [RFC6101] is not\n   sufficiently secure.  This document requires that SSLv3 not be used.\n   The replacement versions, in particular Transport Layer Security\n   (TLS) 1.2 [RFC5246], are considerably more secure and capable\n   protocols.\n\n   This document updates the backward compatibility section of RFC 5246\n   and its predecessors to prohibit fallback to SSLv3.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-sslv3-diediedie/", "expires": "2015-10-12T19:46:09Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 76181, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-sslv3-diediedie", "note": "", "notify": "\"Joseph A. Salowey\" <joe@salowey.net>", "pages": 6, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/76181/", "rev": "03", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/joe@salowey.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/10/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2015-04-13T18:02:46Z", "title": "Deprecating Secure Sockets Layer Version 3.0", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Secure Sockets Layer version 3.0 (SSLv3) [RFC6101] is not\n   sufficiently secure.  This document requires that SSLv3 not be used.\n   The replacement versions, in particular Transport Layer Security\n   (TLS) 1.2 [RFC5246], are considerably more secure and capable\n   protocols.\n\n   This document updates the backward compatibility section of RFC 5246\n   and its predecessors to prohibit fallback to SSLv3.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-sslv3-diediedie/", "expires": "2015-10-12T19:46:09Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 76243, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-sslv3-diediedie", "note": "", "notify": "\"Joseph A. Salowey\" <joe@salowey.net>", "pages": 6, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/76243/", "rev": "03", "rfc_number": null,